  {
   "id": "crush-concurrency-md-15",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Engines\n\nThe native VM (`crush run`) runs tasks and `parallel_map` workers; the portable\nVM (the browser build) runs the same programs with the same output, running\n`parallel_map` items one after another. The AOT backends refuse `spawn` by name\ninstead of dropping it: `` `spawn` (green tasks) isn't supported on the Rust AOT\nbackend yet (#161) ``. See [Engines and AOT](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/engines.html).\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- **[Closures and Function Values](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/closures.html)**\n- **[Engines and AOT](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/engines.html)**\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  }
 ]
